body:
TermAl task-sync regular exchange (Fable2, 2026-11-15, aligned with Engram::Fable #8025).

OWNER: the integration owner, Termal::Opus2, runs TermAl's Central export and push. Fable2 coordinates.

CADENCE:
- at coordinator session start;
- after each TermAl landing;
- before ending work;
- on demand.

FORM:
- tasks planning-only: NO --origin-machine, notes off;
- memories INCLUDED, since 2026-11-15 about 21:05Z (see below);
- privacy re-scan before each commit, with the accepted findings: user paths, and the Windows B LAN hostname or IP in completed items. For memories, also delta-scan every key or revision created or changed since the previous export;
- commit only .engram/* in MAIN/.engram-data;
- fast-forward push of origin engram-data with an explicit refspec, never force;
- save the basis privately under target/task-sync/.
Authority: the task-sync data-branch bullet in CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md (w-e7c5b9511ee3).

MEMORY EXPORT HOLD: LIFTED. w-f70e278d6e7c, the privacy review of every TermAl memory and every revision, is DONE: independent evaluation 3/3, seal 79deed7d, 2026-11-15 20:51:38Z. Final census 483 keys and 1120 revisions. Four re-keys, one citation repointed, one finding declined (the DL560 SSH alias, an accepted operational name).

DL560 IMPORT: s4, under coordinator exceptions cited by message number (s4's log holds the numbering). The DL560 TermAl memory seed follows the first memory export, as its own s4 job under a new exception.

AGENT CONTEXT RULE (Greg, 2026-11-15, Asistant #1822): ordinary listing, search, recovery and reads show only the CURRENT version of each memory; history only by explicit choice. Kimi verified the TermAl paths comply (#325).

REFRESH SEQUENCE (Opus2, 2026-11-15 21:07Z; Engram::Fable #989), proven on the first memory export, commit ba316e29. Export refuses to write over an occupied .engram (task_sync_destination_occupied), so each refresh goes, from the TermAl root with D = .engram-data:
(1) check HEAD = origin/engram-data, MERGE_HEAD empty and a clean status;
(2) cp D/.engram/project.json target/task-sync/central-basis-<HEAD8>.json;
(3) git -C D ls-tree --name-only HEAD .engram/ and note any entries other than project.json and tasks;
(4) git -C D check-ignore -v --no-index .engram/memories/x/head.json must print nothing;
(5) git -C D rm -r -q .engram;
(6) engram task-sync export D/.engram --include-memories --json, with no --origin-machine and no --include-notes. On failure: git -C D restore --source=HEAD --staged --worktree -- .engram, and stop;
(7) restore the step-3 extras with checkout HEAD;
(8) copy the new project.json as the next private basis;
(9) git add .engram; staged paths must be only .engram/project.json, tasks/ and memories/; the receipt must show memories.withheld empty;
(10) disclosure-scan every added line (helper .tmp/q8111/disclosure-scan.mjs), commit, fetch, check that FETCH_HEAD is an ancestor, then git push origin <commit>:refs/heads/engram-data, fast-forward only, and verify with ls-remote.
Note: the commit can block for minutes in git's automatic gc/prune on the shared repository, so run it in the background. Retired keys export as tombstone head.json only, with no body.

ENGRAM BUILD NOTE (Fable2 #6473, 2026-11-15 21:21Z): from Engram w-0349 (89e269f6, installed on Central at 21:20Z), export REFUSES an invalid or missing committed memory envelope, where the earlier build treated the basis as empty. The committed TermAl export ba316e29 was made by the previous build with memories included, so the next routine export should find a valid envelope. If it refuses, STOP and send the refusal to Engram::Fable; never work around it.
